WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.040
- Well, now you're in the
final season of "This Is Us."

00:00:02.040 --> 00:00:04.210
So, what's going on with
your character Rebecca?

00:00:04.210 --> 00:00:05.785
- Oh, way to bring it down.

00:00:05.785 --> 00:00:06.618
(Kelly laughing)

00:00:06.618 --> 00:00:08.160
So, we're tying up,

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:10.440
you know over a 100 episodes of this show,

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:12.040
and telling the story of this family,

00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:13.800
and my character.

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:18.800
Present day, obviously, I
play this woman from 25 to 85.

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:22.020
In present day, she's due with
dementia with Alzheimer's.

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:24.450
So, it's quite heartbreaking,

00:00:24.450 --> 00:00:27.140
but I love that we're able
to have this conversation,

00:00:27.140 --> 00:00:29.830
and hopefully, destigmatize
the conversation

00:00:29.830 --> 00:00:30.780
around Alzheimer's,

00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:34.080
and including the family
and all of the the decisions

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:35.390
that like everyone as a unit,

00:00:35.390 --> 00:00:37.230
collectively has to make together.

00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:38.680
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:42.410
- I'm so excited that we get
to sort of wrap up this story

00:00:42.410 --> 00:00:43.410
in a really beautiful way.

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:46.730
And I think people are
gonna be happy with us

00:00:46.730 --> 00:00:49.000
the way we stick the landing as it were.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:50.170
- Yeah. Is it?

00:00:50.170 --> 00:00:51.760
I have a question 'cause is it hard

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:53.850
to snap out of that when you leave work?

00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:56.930
'Cause y'all do cover so
many serious situations

00:00:56.930 --> 00:00:58.930
and scenarios within family dynamics.

00:00:58.930 --> 00:01:01.980
Is that hard to like
compartmentalize when you go home?

00:01:01.980 --> 00:01:02.900
- I think like for me,

00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:04.730
especially in this particular situation,

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:07.090
like I grieve for my character.

00:01:07.090 --> 00:01:10.210
My character is very
intentional, she's very stoic.

00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:11.200
She has so much grace,

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:13.890
the way she's sort of
handling this diagnosis.

00:01:13.890 --> 00:01:17.690
And I as Mandy, have to not
let my feelings for her,

00:01:17.690 --> 00:01:19.700
my sadness, my grief,

00:01:19.700 --> 00:01:21.560
kind of bleed into the performance.

00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:25.100
So, it's like I'll sometimes
leave set and get back,

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:28.880
you know, to my trailer or in
my car and just like, "Ugh!"

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:30.040
It's an emotional release.

00:01:30.040 --> 00:01:33.680
But also, there's so much
levity in between takes,

00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:35.090
everybody's so funny on the show.

00:01:35.090 --> 00:01:37.530
Like we do find ways to sort
of like crack jokes in between,

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:40.720
'cause otherwise it would be
a horrible work environment.

00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:41.817
- Everybody's just sad?
- Exactly.

00:01:41.817 --> 00:01:43.520
Just crying all the time.

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:45.820
So yeah, ye have to find
a way to like liven it up.

00:01:45.820 --> 00:01:47.450
- Yeah, I love your cast.

00:01:47.450 --> 00:01:48.980
We've had almost everybody on here.

00:01:48.980 --> 00:01:49.813
We love your cast.

00:01:49.813 --> 00:01:50.930
- It's the most remarkable group of people

00:01:50.930 --> 00:01:52.880
I feel so lucky that I've been,

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:54.700
like spent the last six
years of my life with them.

00:01:54.700 --> 00:01:56.180
I love them so deeply.

00:01:56.180 --> 00:01:57.900
- And that's awesome.
- Yeah, they're the best.

00:01:57.900 --> 00:01:59.220
- Well, what has it meant to you,

00:01:59.220 --> 00:02:01.670
that y'all shown so much
diversity on the show?

00:02:01.670 --> 00:02:03.130
Especially within a
family, like one family.

00:02:03.130 --> 00:02:04.780
- Yeah, the family dynamics,

00:02:04.780 --> 00:02:06.450
but what a family can look like.

00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:09.330
I mean I'm so grateful again
that we've had the opportunity

00:02:09.330 --> 00:02:11.230
that people have been
interested in the show

00:02:11.230 --> 00:02:12.750
from the very beginning.

00:02:12.750 --> 00:02:14.120
And have kind of come along

00:02:14.120 --> 00:02:16.790
on this journey with us
for the last six years.

00:02:16.790 --> 00:02:18.870
I think it's the conversations

00:02:18.870 --> 00:02:21.410
we've been able to
elicit are so important.

00:02:21.410 --> 00:02:23.090
Yeah, it's been the greatest gift

00:02:23.090 --> 00:02:25.260
to be a part of something
that's so cathartic,

00:02:25.260 --> 00:02:28.170
and emotional, and also reflective of,

00:02:28.170 --> 00:02:30.110
even though there's so much specificity

00:02:30.110 --> 00:02:32.630
in who these people are in
these different stories,

00:02:32.630 --> 00:02:34.880
people are still able
to see themselves in it,

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:36.360
and that's such a gift.
- [Kelly] Oh, yeah.

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:37.600
Yeah, that is a gift.

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:38.630
Be a part of something that means-

00:02:38.630 --> 00:02:40.097
- Yeah, that means something to people.

00:02:40.097 --> 00:02:40.930
(audience clapping)

00:02:40.930 --> 00:02:42.179
- Well, thank you so much, Mandy.

00:02:42.179 --> 00:02:43.012
We love having you on.
- Thank you.

00:02:43.012 --> 00:02:43.920
So good to see you.

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:45.910
- [Kelly] You can see the
final season of "This Is Us,"

00:02:45.910 --> 00:02:46.753
Tuesdays on NBC.

